{"text": "ECF,PRO-SE\n\nU.S. District Court\nSouthern District of New York (Foley Square)\nCIVIL DOCKET FOR CASE #: 1:22-cv-00044\u2014-AJN\n\nSmolen v. The Federal Aviation Administration\n\nAssigned to: Judge Alison J. Nathan\nCause: 05:552 Freedom of Information Act\n\nDate Filed: 01/04/2022\nJury Demand: None\nNature of Suit: 895 Freedom of\n\nPlaintiff\n\nRobert E. Smolen\n\nV.\nDefendant\n\nInformation Act\nJurisdiction: Federal Question\n\nrepresented by Robert E. Smolen\n338 Curtis Ave.\nCarle Place, NY 11514\n516 491 0465\nEmail: robert_smolen@hotmail.com\nPRO SE\n\nThe Federal Aviation Administration\n\nDate Filed\n\nDocket Text\n\n01/04/2022\n\nCOMPLAINT against The Federal Aviation Administration. (Filing Fee $ 402.00,\nReceipt Number 465401291612)Document filed by Robert E. Smolen..(rdz) (Entered:\n01/04/2022)\n\n01/04/2022\n\nCase Designated ECF. (rdz) (Entered: 01/04/2022)\n\n01/04/2022\n\nMagistrate Judge Barbara C. Moses is so designated. Pursuant to 28 U.S.C. Section\n636(c) and Fed. R. Civ. P. 73(b)(1) parties are notified that they may consent to\nproceed before a United States Magistrate Judge. Parties who wish to consent may\naccess the necessary form at the following link:\n\nhttps://nysd.uscourts.gov/sites/default/files/2018\u201406/AO-3.pdf. (rdz) (Entered:\n01/04/2022)\n\n01/07/2022\n\nREQUEST FOR ISSUANCE OF SUMMONS as to Federal Aviation Administration,\nre: 1 Complaint. Document filed by Robert E. Smolen. (sc) (Entered: 01/07/2022)\n\n01/07/2022\n\nTransmission to Pro Se Assistants. Transmitted re: 3 Request for Issuance of Summons\nto the Pro Se Assistants for processing. (sc) (Entered: 01/07/2022)\n\n01/07/2022\n\neS\n\nSUMMONS ISSUED as to The Federal Aviation Administration. (aan) (Entered:\n01/07/2022)\n\n01/07/2022\n\nMailed a copy of 4 Summons Issued to Robert E. Smolen 338 Curtis Ave. Carle Place,\nNY 11514. (aan) (Entered: 01/07/2022)\n\n01/10/2022\n\nIn\n\nORDER OF SERVICE: Plaintiff, who is proceeding pro se, paid the filing fees to\ncommence this action. The Clerk of Court issued a summons as to Defendant Federal\nAviation Administration on January 7, 2022. Dkt. No. 4. Plaintiff is directed to serve\nthe summons and complaint on Defendant within 90 days of the issuance of the\nsummons. If within those 90 days, Plaintiff has not either served Defendant or\nrequested an extension of time to do so, the Court may dismiss the claims against\nDefendant under Rules 4 and 41 of the Federal Rules of Civil Procedure for failure to\nprosecute. The Clerk of Court is directed to mail an information package to Plaintiff.\nPlaintiff has consented to receive electronic service of notices and documents in this\naction. (ECF 1, at 9.) SO ORDERED. (Signed by Judge Alison J. Nathan on\n1/10/2022) (vfr) Transmission to Pro Se Assistants for processing. (Entered:\n01/10/2022)",
